/target
/docs/book
/crates/pyrographer-gui/dist
**/*.rs.bk

# Vendor blobs and hardware-campaign artifacts. These are Rockchip's own
# proprietary loaders and U-Boot builds, or byproducts of driving them against
# real hardware -- none of them are ours to publish, and this repository is
# MIT/Apache. They are fenced here so a `git add -A` cannot sweep them into a
# public tree. Keep them out of the repo (or move them out entirely); the code
# reads the reference loader from an out-of-tree `reference/` directory.
#
# Any `.bin` dropped at the repo root is treated as a vendor blob: they keep
# appearing here (u-boot-rockchip-*.bin, rk3576_*.bin, ...). This is anchored to
# the root on purpose -- captured hardware *test fixtures* live under `crates/`,
# and are not fenced.
/*.bin
/*.tar.gz
/maskrom-uboot-experiment/
/reference/

# Local experiment tooling and working notes, kept out of the published tree by
# default. Move one in deliberately if it earns a place; it does not belong
# in-tree just because `git add -A` would take it.
/dump-factory.sh
/verify-dump.py
/RK3576UBOOT.ini

# A machine-to-machine transfer checklist: which files to copy to the flash kit on
# the other machine, and their checksums. Every artifact it names is fenced above,
# so the note is a list of things this repository refuses to ship, addressed to one
# person's laptop.
/SYNC-TO-FLASHKIT.md

# The exploratory patch behind the finding in internal_docs/architecture.md that
# nusb's own WebUSB backend can carry everything except a transfer's deadline and
# its cancellation. The finding is what is documented; this is the experiment that
# produced it, and a patch against a moving tree rots where prose does not.
/nusb-webusb-prototype.patch
